Added option to java client to send query with CompletableFuture response. It allows work in a functional style with asynchronous requests, as well as chaining and combining.
```
// with Optional check
client.send(new TdApi.GetMe()).thenAccept(response ->
        response.object().ifPresentOrElse(
                me -> System.out.println("I'm " + me.firstName + " " + me.lastName),
                () -> System.out.println(response.error().orElseGet(TdApi.Error::new))
        )
);

// with callbacks
client.send(new TdApi.GetMe())
        .thenAccept(response -> response
                .onSuccess(me -> System.out.println("I'm " + me.firstName + " " + me.lastName))
                .onError(System.out::println)
        );
```

Because of CompletableFuture available since java 1.8, minimum supported version has been updated too.

### Description
When trying to extend styled components, the VM is crashing and dropping the following error:
<img width="569" alt="image" src="https://github.com/NearSocial/VM/assets/47929792/3f8afeb9-deb8-4d1e-bab7-3f47ef3199b4">

### Issue
When the VM is parsing the element and asserting whether it is a Radix component or not, it doesn't handle the scenario when the property is an object. Because of this, when checking if the value is falsy, it doesn't stop the function flow and treats it as a string, leading to the `e.split` error dropping, and stopping the whole application.
```js
// vm.js
const assertRadixComponent = (element) => {
  if (!element) return;
```

### Solution
Asserting that the element is of type `string` before continuing the assertion process, on the `VM::assertRadixComponent(element)` method:
```js
// vm.js
const assertRadixComponent = (element) => {
  if (!element || typeof element !== "string") return;
```
